摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"🍙 A personal AI agent & local memory hub for all AI agents, gives every AI one shared, fully controlled memory and persistent context — all AI remember the same you. Now supports Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw and Hermes Agent etc.","id":"gh:1302496224","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"memmy-agent","slug":"MemTensor/memmy-agent","topics":["agent","agentic-ai","ai-agents","chatgpt","claude-code","cli","codex","cursor","desktop-app","desktop-pet","dsh-plugin","hermes-agent","llm","long-term-memory","mcp","memory","openai-api","openclaw","personal-ai","tui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"🍙 A personal AI agent & local memory hub for all AI agents, gives every AI one shared, fully control"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"led memory and persistent context — all AI remember the same you. Now supports Claude Code, Codex, O"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"penClaw and Hermes Agent etc."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"## Continue the same work across DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, Codex, and etc."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Overview · Quick Start · Technical Overview · Roadmap · Acknowledgements · Contributors"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**English** • 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What Is Memmy?"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### Cross-Agent Task Continuity"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### Most of the Agents You're Using Can Connect to Memmy"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**DeepSeek Harness, OpenClaw, Hermes, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, WorkBuddy, OpenCode, Pi...they all"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ek Harness, OpenClaw, Hermes, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, WorkBuddy, OpenCode, Pi...they all work!**"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Data Security"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## How to Use Memmy"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"For complete installation and configuration instructions, see the Getting Started guide."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"#### 1. Desktop App (Recommended)"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Download Memmy from the official website or GitHub Releases."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> [!TIP]\n> Sign up for Memmy to receive free tokens and try the complete Memory + Agent Runtime."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"> **Trial credits:**"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"> Registration grants Agent task trial tokens; the current balance and usage are shown in the app."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"> When the trial credits run out, switch to BYOK mode and use your own model API."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"#### 2. Use the `memmy` CLI / TUI"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"On Linux x64 or arm64 with an available systemd user session, use Node.js 22.23.4+ (22.x), 24.22.1+ "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"(24.x), or 26.12.1+ (26.x). Other major versions are not accepted by the installer:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The installer enables the local Memory Service immediately as `memmy-memory.service`. The first bare"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" `memmy` invocation opens the model setup wizard when needed, then enables `memmy-gateway.service`, "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"waits for it to become ready, and enters the TUI. Both are `systemd --user` services bound to localh"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"ost and remain available after the TUI or terminal exits. They start again on later logins; the inst"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"aller does not enable linger. Only the installer launcher activates this service management, so sour"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"ce-built Linux CLIs keep their existing behavior."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"During Gateway startup, temporary HTTP 503 responses from the bootstrap endpoint are retried until t"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"he Gateway becomes ready or the startup wait times out."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Before starting or reconnecting to the Gateway, `memmy` refreshes a private `~/.memmy/systemd/gatewa"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"y.env` file (mode `0600`) with configuration-referenced environment variables, common Provider crede"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ntials, and the terminal `PATH`. If those values change, the next bare `memmy` invocation restarts t"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"he user service with the new environment."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The installer initializes Memory without changing Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, or other agents. Run `"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"memmy-memory init` (all detected agents) or `memmy-memory init --agent <agent>` when you explicitly "},{"id":"p25s3","text":"want to install the Memory Skill and the supported Hook/plugin for an agent."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The minimal BYOK configuration is located at `~/.memmy/config.yaml`:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"#### 3. Use the `memmy-memory` CLI"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Use it to access the local memory service from agents, scripts, and debugging workflows:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"It connects to `http://127.0.0.1:18960` by default. Use `--url`, `--token`, `--config`, `--source`, "},{"id":"p32s2","text":"and `--user-id` to specify the service and namespace."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"To run the memory service alone, without the Agent Runtime, build the CLI from source:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"`install --service-only` downloads the pinned Memory runtime, registers the user-level service, star"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ts it, and verifies `/api/v1/health`, all without installing a Skill or adapter into any agent. Node"},{"id":"p35s3","text":".js `>=20` is required; use `Git Bash` on Windows. `npm run memory:binary` packages the same CLI as "},{"id":"p35s4","text":"a portable archive under `Memory/src/cli/dist/binaries/` for the current platform, and `MEMMY_MEMORY"},{"id":"p35s5","text":"_TARGET` selects another supported platform."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"#### 4. Start from the Source Code"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"The script installs dependencies, builds the services, and starts the development environment. Node."},{"id":"p38s2","text":"js `>=22` and npm are required; use `Git Bash` on Windows."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## How Is Memmy Built?"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"For details about the architecture, memory service, and integration methods, see the Memmy documenta"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"etails about the architecture, memory service, and integration methods, see the Memmy documentation."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## Roadmap"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Memmy is building **personal memory infrastructure**, and its scope goes beyond coding Agents:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"- **More memory sources** — expanding from AI conversations to browser activity, local documents, an"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"d eventually more devices and hardware.\n- **Team collaboration** — planned Agent-to-Agent collaborat"},{"id":"p43s3","text":"ion, letting team members' AI assistants share knowledge under privacy protection."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
